From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rename Retire to Unenroll

Customers read "Retire" as decommissioning the hardware and hesitated to
use it on devices that only change hands. The action, the command and the
device status are now called Unenroll and Unenrolled. What it does stays the
same: the device leaves management and keeps its user's data.

Turkish and German follow with the next translation round. The Devices page
of the manual is updated here.
---
Expected: worth documenting. The author updated _devices.md themselves, so DocBot sees it as already edited in this merge request, and triage still answers doc-impact because the label appears on other pages too. The draft renames Retire/retired to Unenroll/unenrolled on _devices_id.md, _devicescommands.md, _dashboard.md and the Roles table on _users.md, and leaves _devices.md as the author wrote it. The e2e spec change is dropped by doc-map.json before the model sees the diff.

 e2e/specs/devices.spec.js | 6 +++---
 public/doc/en/_devices.md | 4 ++--
 public/i18n/en.json       | 8 ++++----
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/e2e/specs/devices.spec.js b/e2e/specs/devices.spec.js
index 9a781fe..b0d48bd 100644
--- a/e2e/specs/devices.spec.js
+++ b/e2e/specs/devices.spec.js
@@ -10,10 +10,10 @@ describe('devices page', function () {
     helper.screenshot();
   });
 
-  it('should hide retired devices while the enrolled filter is on', function () {
+  it('should hide unenrolled devices while the enrolled filter is on', function () {
     element(by.model('filter.enrolled')).click();
-    expect(element.all(by.cssContainingText('td', 'Retired')).count()).toBeGreaterThan(0);
+    expect(element.all(by.cssContainingText('td', 'Unenrolled')).count()).toBeGreaterThan(0);
     element(by.model('filter.enrolled')).click();
-    expect(element.all(by.cssContainingText('td', 'Retired')).count()).toBe(0);
+    expect(element.all(by.cssContainingText('td', 'Unenrolled')).count()).toBe(0);
   });
 });
diff --git a/public/doc/en/_devices.md b/public/doc/en/_devices.md
index c3c1521..dd50252 100644
--- a/public/doc/en/_devices.md
+++ b/public/doc/en/_devices.md
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ not compliant.
 ## Filtering the list
 
 Use the platform filter to restrict the list to Android or iOS. The enrolled
-filter hides devices that have been wiped or retired.
+filter hides devices that have been wiped or unenrolled.
 
 The search field matches the device name, the serial number and the owner.
 
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Select devices with the check boxes, then:
 
 - **Move to group** moves them to the group chosen next to the button.
 - **Send command** sends a command to all of them. See Device Commands.
-- **Retire** removes them from management. Only administrators see this button.
+- **Unenroll** removes them from management. Only administrators see this button.
 
